# Summary
Introduced: the commit adds HistoryEntry fields for DiscordToken and DiscordMessageID, populates them from upload results, and persists them to a newly created history.json using world-readable file permissions.
The new history feature persists Discord deletion metadata, including DiscordWebhookID, DiscordToken, and DiscordMessageID, for every successful upload. SaveHistory writes history.json with mode 0644 and creates its parent directory with 0755, making the file readable by other local users on platforms where POSIX modes apply and by any process/account that can access the app directory. A reader of this file can recover Discord webhook bearer tokens plus message IDs for historical uploads, enabling unauthorized posting to the webhook and deletion of recorded Discord messages. The data is also included in UI state/results even though the frontend only needs opaque history IDs to request deletion, increasing exposure to any renderer compromise or accidental state disclosure.

# Validation
## Rubric
- [x] Sensitive Discord deletion metadata is represented in serializable structs with JSON fields.
- [x] The upload/processing path populates Result/HistoryEntry with webhook token, webhook ID, and message ID.
- [x] SaveHistory writes the metadata to history.json using broad permissions, specifically 0755 for directories and 0644 for the file.
- [x] A dynamic PoC using the real appcore functions confirms the token/message ID are written to disk and the resulting file has mode 0644 under the default umask.
- [x] The same sensitive values are exposed to frontend/API state through UIState Results/History.
## Report
Validated the finding with targeted code review plus a dynamic PoC using the real Go functions. Rubric results are included below. Key code evidence: src/internal/appcore/history.go:13-23 defines HistoryEntry with discordMessageId, discordWebhookId, and discordToken JSON fields; src/internal/appcore/history.go:52-60 writes history.json after MkdirAll(..., 0755) and WriteFile(..., 0644); src/internal/appcore/history.go:63-88 copies Discord metadata from Result into HistoryEntry and saves it; src/internal/appcore/processor.go:91-102 copies UploadDiscord output into Result; src/internal/appcore/discord.go:30-88 parses the webhook token from the webhook URL and returns it with the Discord message ID; src/internal/appcore/types.go:12-18 includes full HistoryEntry objects in UIState, and app.go:199-202 / 236-240 places history and results into state. Dynamic reproduction: I added src/validation_poc/main.go, which runs an httptest fake Discord webhook, calls appcore.UploadDiscord, then appcore.AddResultsToHistory/SaveHistory. Command `cd /workspace/ClipForVRChat/src && go run ./validation_poc` produced: history_dir_mode=0755, history_file_mode=0644, persisted_contains_token=true, persisted_contains_message_id=true, ui_state_contains_token=true, followed by history.json containing `"discordMessageId":"MSG_SECRET_123"`, `"discordWebhookId":"WEBHOOK_PUBLIC_456"`, and `"discordToken":"TOKEN_SECRET_ABC"`. The environment umask was 0022. I also verified local cross-account readability in the constructed reachable app directory: `su nobody -s /bin/sh -c 'head -c 120 /tmp/clipforvrchat-history-poc/appconfig/history.json'` successfully printed the beginning of history.json. Crash/Valgrind/debugger attempts: this is not a crash-class bug; a debug build/run completed normally and demonstrated the issue. Valgrind and gdb/dlv were not installed, so memory-check/debugger traces were unavailable and not applicable to this information disclosure.

